National Address Database (NAD)
-------------------------------
Files: extdata/nad_39061.rds, extdata/nad_39061_mp.rds,
       extdata/v2/nad_catalog/23/counties.parquet
Provider: U.S. Department of Transportation, with state, local, and tribal
          address programs.
Source: National Address Database, revision 23.
        https://data.transportation.gov/d/fc2s-wawr
Preparation: The address fixture contains 5,000 Hamilton County, Ohio rows;
             the prepared index is derived from that fixture. The catalog
             inventories revision 23 source county labels and row counts.
Terms: USDOT identifies the NAD as a federal government work not subject to
       copyright protection under 17 U.S.C. 105 and available for reuse
       without limitation or restriction. Its disclaimer also describes
       accuracy, coverage, liability, and state mailing-list limitations.
       https://www.transportation.gov/mission/open/gis/national-address-database/national-address-database-nad-disclaimer
Attribution: U.S. Department of Transportation, National Address Database,
             revision 23; county fixture and matching index prepared by the
             addr authors.

Address-string examples (historical function name: voter_addresses)
-------------------------------------------------------------------
File: extdata/voter_addresses.rds
Provider: U.S. Department of Transportation, National Address Database.
Source: The packaged Hamilton County NAD revision 23 fixture described above.
Preparation: inst/make_address_examples.R formats that fixture and retains the
             first 2,000 unique strings, in source order. The function name is
             retained for compatibility; the current fixture is not voter data.
Terms and attribution: The same unrestricted USDOT reuse terms and attribution
                       as the National Address Database section above.
Historical provenance: Earlier versions used Hamilton County Board of Elections
                       voter addresses from a 2024-09-12 export. That fixture
                       was replaced because no redistribution license or
                       separate written permission had been established.
                       The old URL is retained only as plain-text provenance:
  https://votehamiltoncountyohio.gov/download.php?file=VoterListExport-20240912-no.csv

Cincinnati Eviction Hotspots
-----------------------------
File: extdata/elh_data.rds
Provider: Eviction Lab, Princeton University.
Source: Eviction Tracking System, Cincinnati hotspot report for 2022-09-01
        through 2023-08-31, retrieved 2026-10-30 from the provider's licensed
        download archive:
  https://eviction-lab-data-downloads.s3.amazonaws.com/ets/hotspots_reports.zip
Archive member: hotspots_reports/cincinnati_hotspots_media_report.csv
Preparation: inst/make_elh_data.R converts that CSV to a tibble with Date
             columns and saves all 100 rows and nine columns in RDS format.
             Values and row order are otherwise unchanged. The RDS includes
             source, attribution, and license attributes.
Terms: Open Data Commons Attribution License (ODC-BY) 1.0. The provider's
       download site identifies eviction-lab-data-downloads as its data bucket
       and explicitly offers its data under ODC-BY 1.0; its /ets directory
       contains this hotspot archive.
  https://data-downloads.evictionlab.org/
  https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/by/1-0/
       The database is redistributed under ODC-BY 1.0, not the package's MIT
       software license. A complete copy is installed as ODC-BY-1.0.
       Redistribution must preserve attribution and license notices and include
       this license or its URI. Publicly used outputs must identify the source
       database and its ODC-BY license (sections 4.2-4.4). The license permits
       commercial use, copying, modification, and redistribution (section 3.1).
Attribution: Contains information from the Eviction Lab, Princeton University,
             Eviction Tracking System, Cincinnati hotspot report for
             2022-09-01 through 2023-08-31, made available under ODC-BY 1.0.
Provider's requested collection citation (2026; not the snapshot's date):
  Peter Hepburn, Adam Chapnik, Danny Grubbs-Donovan, Jacob Haas, Grace Hartley,
  Olivia Jin, Sarah Johnson, Renee Louis, Jasmine Rangel, Salar Safarkhani,
  and Matthew Desmond. Eviction Tracking System: Version 4.0. Princeton:
